    },
    "body": "## Summary\n- replace wildcard WebSocket handshake origins with a configurable trusted-origin policy\n- reject a global `*` origin at startup while preserving safe localhost defaults for development\n- apply the same allowlist to native STOMP and SockJS endpoints\n- document the production configuration variable\n- add backend unit coverage for parsing, deduplication and unsafe wildcard rejection\n\n## Why\nLive courier tracking already authorizes `/topic/tracking/{jobId}` subscriptions to active job participants. This hardens the handshake layer as well, reducing cross-origin exposure for location-bearing realtime channels.\n\n## Validation\nGitHub-hosted CI is requested on this PR. The execution environment available to this run cannot resolve github.com for a local clone, so no local Maven invocation is claimed here; the PR must remain unmerged unless CI passes.",
